FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:5069 — `edge_constant_module_member_write_replaces_the_published_function` feeds `constant M.f to 2` to the LSP and asserts member replacement, but `src/parser.rs:796-819` only accepts a single `Identifier` after `constant` and then requires `to`; the `.` makes this a `ParserError`. The test therefore pins navigation for source the language cannot parse, and it exercises the unreachable `TokenKind::Constant` member-write branch in `src/lsp.rs:1903-1923`. Remove the fixture and the constant member-write branch, or add parser/SPEC support for constant member targets if that is intended. — VERIFIED: read `src/parser.rs:799-816`; `parse_constant` reads one identifier and calls `expect(TokenKind::To)`.
2. [MAJOR] src/lsp.rs:1987-1998 — the `set` reuse search walks every live scope, including the program root, so a variable declared before a `module` body is reused as the module's published value binding and then recorded by `src/lsp.rs:2059-2072`. That makes `M.name` goto/references point at and merge with the outer program variable, contradicting the phase's stated module-frame model. The new fixture at tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:5353 only covers a same-named variable declared *after* the module, so it does not exercise this ordering. Fix: bound the `set` reuse search to the current runtime frame chain, and add a fixture with `set count to 99` before `module M`. What would settle it: run that fixture against the analyzer/VM and compare with `goto_definition`/`find_references`.
3. [MINOR] tests/module_system_test.rs:266-284 — the new “constant is a global” golden test only inspects `vm.module_member_values("M")`; it never reads `label` after `end`, so it pins the “not published” half but not the “program global” half claimed by its name. Add an assertion that `label` is still readable in the program scope after the module closes.
4. [MINOR] phases/phase-075/REPORT.md:199-214 — the re-harvested gate count does not reconcile: from 2897, the described additions (5 module-value tests + 2 round-3 + 2 round-2) total 9 and reach 2906, not 2911; the paragraph also calls the last additions “round-2” after the “round-3” tests. Re-harvest `cargo test --all-targets` and list the exact new test instances that make up 2911.

